Context: an independent reviewer (another AI session) reviewed the branch at commit 8c1107e and wrote a report in Russian: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-<user>-Development-taxdome-ta-firm-payments-challenge/34fb75aa-e848-4899-b380-313c497e2654/scratchpad/review-report.md. The author then settled the findings: fix finding 6 (check the payment count before validating items), add a test for /healthz 503 and exclude /healthz from A12 in the spec (finding 5), document finding 4 with remedies including anyio.CapacityLimiter, keep /docs,/redoc,/openapi.json and describe them (finding 8), and correct docs disproved by findings 3 and 7.

The full change against 8c1107e (two commits plus uncommitted doc edits) is in: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-<user>-Development-taxdome-ta-firm-payments-challenge/34fb75aa-e848-4899-b380-313c497e2654/scratchpad/triage.diff

Your job: check every factual claim ADDED or CHANGED in that diff against (a) the code and tests in the working tree and (b) the review report. Examples of what to verify:
- numbers attributed to the review (9 of 10, 3 of 10, 12 of 13 = 3 own runs + 9 of 10, 14 s, 45 requests, 5.0–10.0 s, 13.06 s, 2.97 s, 4999998 / 50002, acceptance values, 10/11/9) match the report;
- test counts (162 total; unit 65, db 14, api 65, concurrency 18) — verify with `uv run --locked pytest --collect-only -q` (collection does not need the database);
- names of tests cited (e.g. test names, C7 being "C1, C2 and I5 over HTTP", I1/I8 byte-identical replay tests, C4 reading the committed balance, the statement-order test) exist and do what the text claims;
- the claims about the code: payment count checked by a before-validator in app/schemas.py with a single too_long detail; /healthz body; 400→422 mapping in app/main.py; 307 on trailing slash (FastAPI redirect_slashes default — check whether the request log in app/main.py would skip it); `status` field in the log record;
- that no edited sentence contradicts another part of README.md, docs/spec.md, docs/verification-notes.md or docs/plan.md (e.g. limitation numbering referenced as "limitation 15", spec "section 15, item 15");
- markdown structure: tables not broken, list numbering consistent.
Also review the code change itself (app/schemas.py, app/service.py, the tests) for correctness bugs: e.g. does removing the check from build_command leave any caller (scripts/load.py, tests/concurrency/conftest.py, etc.) without the limit; does calling get_settings() inside a validator break anything.

Report: a numbered list of concrete discrepancies, each with file:line, what the text says, what is true, and a suggested correction. Then a one-line list of what you verified as correct. No praise, no general advice. Keep it under 700 words.

